#279 lifetime-tty hook transport correction — Sable Embertail <EXECUTOR>
2026-10-24; Oracle0396ea76-9a1a-4bfa-b042-a0812f0cfa3a.

The hook shim originally accepts an OSC write to any controlling tty as delivery. A service lifetime tty has no output consumer, so that fast path could swallow hooks. RuntimePlan selects BBOXY_HOOK_SOCKET_ONLY=1 only for the side service, and the shim uses its caller-supplied authenticated sink under that flag. Ordinary PTY hooks retain OSC.

The regression uses two actual private tty children: the ordinary child writes an OSC7502 frame; the socket-only child must write no tty bytes and must call the supplied sink with SessionStart/session. It adds no proto/supervisor/mux dependency to the kit. The launcher regression asserts only the server env gets the selector.

The first test fixture waited for the session leader to exit before draining its tty, which could hold the child in tty close. Its owned parent36267 was terminated, freeing the master; both fixture PIDs were then absent. The corrected fixture drains while waiting and drops the master before child cleanup on failure. Supervisor stop/Drop also close their lifetime master before waiting, preventing that buffered-output close dependency.

